</node>
<node id="Bank">
  <data key="d0">Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">An institution that maintains accounts for customers and engages in financial transactions, involved in managing customer relationships.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-020</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Bank</data>
</node>
<node id="Savings Account">
  <data key="d0">Savings Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Savings Account is a type of bank account designed for individuals to save money while earning interest on their deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Savings Account</data>
</node>
<node id="Current Account">
  <data key="d0">Current Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Current Account is a type of bank account that allows individuals running a business to manage their transactions consistently with their declared business activities.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of bank account that allows for frequent transactions, withdrawals, and deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Current Account</data>
</node>
<node id="RBI">
  <data key="d0">RBI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">RBI, or Reserve Bank of India, is the central banking institution of India, which regulates the country's monetary policy and oversees the banking sector.&lt;SEP&gt;RBI (Reserve Bank of India) is the central banking institution of India, which regulates the country's monetary policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">RBI</data>
</node>
<node id="KYC">
  <data key="d0">KYC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Know Your Customer (KYC) is a comprehensive process utilized by banks and financial institutions to verify the identity of their clients. This process is crucial for assessing potential risks associated with illegal activities, such as fraud and money laundering. KYC is not merely an operational procedure but a regulatory requirement that mandates banks to adhere to legal standards designed to prevent financial misconduct.

The KYC process involves several key steps, including the verification of customer identities to establish who they are and to ensure compliance with regulatory frameworks. By implementing KYC measures, banks are able to mitigate risks that could arise from fraudulent activities and ensure that they are not inadvertently facilitating illegal operations.

As an acronym for "Know Your Customer," KYC encompasses a set of regulations and procedures that guide banks in identifying their clients. The main goal of KYC is to promote transparency and security in banking practices by ensuring that clientele are properly vetted in accordance with legal and regulatory expectations. Therefore, KYC represents a critical aspect of financial compliance, aimed at protecting both institutions and consumers from the consequences of financial crimes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-016</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627117</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">KYC</data>
</node>
<node id="PAN">
  <data key="d0">PAN</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Permanent Account Number (PAN) is a unique identification number issued by the Indian income tax department for individuals and entities, required for KYC documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;PAN (Permanent Account Number) is a unique identifier issued to individuals, required for various banking processes, including account opening and changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">PAN</data>
</node>
<node id="Minor Account">
  <data key="d0">Minor Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Minor Account is a bank account that can be opened for individuals under 18 years of age, typically requiring a guardian for oversight.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Minor Account</data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Account">
  <data key="d0">Joint Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Joint Account is a type of bank account that is opened by two or more persons in their joint names, allowing shared access and operation of the account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Joint Account</data>
</node>
<node id="Power of Attorney">
  <data key="d0">Power of Attorney</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal document that appoints an agent to make decisions on behalf of the principal, often for larger or more complex transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Power of Attorney (POA) refers to a legal authorization allowing one person to act on behalf of another in legal or financial matters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-010</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Power of Attorney</data>
</node>
<node id="Illiterate Person">
  <data key="d0">Illiterate Person</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who is unable to read or write, requiring special considerations during the account opening process at a bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Illiterate Person</data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian">
  <data key="d0">Guardian</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Guardian is an individual appointed, either naturally or by court order, to manage accounts for minors or individuals unable to handle their financial affairs.&lt;SEP&gt;A guardian is an individual responsible for managing the affairs of a minor, specifically in the context of KYC/CKYC processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A guardian is a person legally designated to care for a minor and manage their financial affairs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Guardian</data>
</node>
<node id="Transgender Person">
  <data key="d0">Transgender Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A transgender person is an individual who identifies as a gender different from the sex assigned at birth and is recognized as 'Third Gender' under financial regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Transgender Person</data>
</node>
<node id="Mental Health Act, 1987">
  <data key="d0">Mental Health Act, 1987</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Mental Health Act, 1987 is a law that outlines the treatment and care provisions for mentally ill persons, including the appointment of guardians and the management of their property.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Mental Health Act, 1987</data>
</node>
<node id="National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999">
  <data key="d0">National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal framework that allows banking accounts to be opened for persons with disabilities by a legally appointed guardian.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999</data>
</node>
<node id="Term Deposit Account">
  <data key="d0">Term Deposit Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Term Deposit Account is a type of savings account where money is deposited for a fixed term at a specified interest rate, typically higher than that of a standard savings account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Term Deposit Account</data>
</node>
<node id="KYC Documents">
  <data key="d0">KYC Documents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">KYC Documents are the identification documents required by Unity Small Finance Bank to verify the identity and address of customers.&lt;SEP&gt;KYC Documents are identification and verification papers required by banks to adhere to KYC regulations, ensuring customer identity verification.&lt;SEP&gt;KYC Documents are necessary identification and verification documents required by the bank to establish the identity of account holders.&lt;SEP&gt;KYC (Know Your Customer) documents are identification documents required by financial institutions to verify the identity of clients, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;KYC Documents (Know Your Customer documents) are mandatory records that verify the identity of bank customers in compliance with regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Documents required to verify the identity of individuals in compliance with Know Your Customer regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Know Your Customer documents required for verifying the identity of clients during account activation and management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">KYC Documents</data>
</node>
<node id="Minor">
  <data key="d0">Minor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A minor is an individual under the age of majority who may hold an account under special conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification indicating the account type for customers, especially in the context of KYC documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Minor</data>
</node>
<node id="Customer">
  <data key="d0">Customer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A resident account holder who maintains either a savings or current account with Unity Bank and is eligible for Doorstep Banking services.&lt;SEP&gt;Customers of Unity Small Finance Bank are individuals or entities seeking financial services and banking relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;A customer is an individual or entity that holds an account or avails banking services from Unity Small Finance Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786627113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Customer</data>
</node>
<node id="Doorstep Banking">
  <data key="d0">Doorstep Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A banking service model allowing banks to provide various services directly at customers' doorsteps, enabling accessibility for residents, especially senior citizens and differently-abled individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unity Bank">
  <data key="d0">Unity Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A bank offering Doorstep Banking services to its customers, allowing ease of access to banking services through deliveries to customers' residences.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senior Citizen">
  <data key="d0">Senior Citizen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refers to elderly individuals who are eligible for specific banking services and savings limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals aged over 60 years who are eligible to utilize Doorstep Banking services provided by Unity Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differently Abled">
  <data key="d0">Differently Abled</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Refers to individuals with disabilities who are eligible for specific banking services and savings limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals with disabilities who are eligible to receive Doorstep Banking services to facilitate their banking needs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Management Vendor">
  <data key="d0">Cash Management Vendor</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A third-party service provider that can be outsourced by banks to manage cash deliveries and pickups for Doorstep Banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Banking Correspondents">
  <data key="d0">Banking Correspondents</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals or entities empaneled with banks to assist in delivering banking services, including Doorstep Banking, to customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TPIN">
  <data key="d0">TPIN</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A secure authentication method used to verify service requests for Doorstep Banking delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Charges">
  <data key="d0">Service Charges</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fees levied on customer accounts for using Doorstep Banking services, subject to a pre-agreed schedule and communicated in advance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Banking Service Savings Limits">
  <data key="d0">Banking Service Savings Limits</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A table that outlines the savings limits associated with different banking services for various customer segments, including individuals, senior citizens, differently abled individuals, and current account customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Pickup">
  <data key="d0">Cash Pickup</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the types of banking services listed in the table, allowing customers to pick up cash.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Delivery">
  <data key="d0">Cash Delivery</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Another type of banking service listed in the table, allowing customers to receive cash through delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Account Customers">
  <data key="d0">Current Account Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals who hold a current account with the bank and have access to higher savings limits for banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001">
  <data key="d0">tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]banking_service_savings_limits

This table outlines the savings limits associated with different banking services for various customer segments. It consists of four columns: 'Type of service', 'Savings (individuals)', 'Senior Citizen / Differently Abled', and 'Current Account Customers'. The table details two types of services, 'Cash Pickup' and 'Cash Delivery', which are available to customers. For both services, the savings limit for individuals is set at 20,000 per instance. Senior citizens and differently abled individuals also have the same limit of 20,000 per instance for these services, denoting support for such groups. Interestingly, current account customers have access to a significantly higher limit of 5 lacs per instance for both service types, which illustrates a disparity in service access based on account type. There are no merged cells present, and all data points are filled without any missing or null values. The information is subject to change per the bank's policy, as noted in the footnote. The context surrounding the table indicates that these services can be offered both by the bank's own staff and through outsourcing to cash management vendors or banking correspondents, emphasizing a flexible operational approach. This table serves as a quick reference for customers to understand the limits on funds that can be accessed through these banking services.

[Table Footnotes]# Subject to change from time to time as per banks policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786618357</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
