<node id="Consumer Banking">
  <data key="d0">Consumer Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consumer Banking refers to the division of Unity Small Finance Bank that focuses on personal accounts and services for individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Consumer Banking refers to banking services provided to individual customers, including the onboarding process for non-individual customers that require pre-approval.&lt;SEP&gt;The department responsible for managing retail customer accounts at Unity Small Finance Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Account Opening">
  <data key="d0">Account Opening</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Account Opening is the procedure followed by Unity Small Finance Bank to set up bank accounts for customers, which includes various regulations and requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;An action documented in the checklist as part of the Purpose of EDD that refers to the initiation of a new bank account for a customer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-015</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enhanced Due Diligence">
  <data key="d0">Enhanced Due Diligence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Enhanced Due Diligence is a process carried out by Unity Small Finance Bank to ensure thorough verification of customer identities and accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;A comprehensive approach to customer verification and risk assessment, particularly relevant in the context of the bank's operational protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;A process that requires additional investigation and information gathering concerning risks associated with financial activities, particularly in banking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-018</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inoperative Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Inoperative Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inoperative Accounts refer to the bank accounts that have had no customer-induced transactions for over two years as per Unity Small Finance Bank's policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Inoperative Accounts refer to bank accounts that have not had any customer-initiated transactions for a specified period, typically leading to special procedures for activation or closure.&lt;SEP&gt;Inoperative accounts refer to accounts that have not had any transactions for a specified period and can be reactivated with appropriate KYC documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aadhaar Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Aadhaar Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Aadhaar Authentication is a method used for customer onboarding at Unity Small Finance Bank through the verification of the Aadhaar identity system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probate of Will">
  <data key="d0">Probate of Will</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">Probate of Will is a legal document required by Unity Small Finance Bank when a guardian is appointed through a testamentary will for opening accounts for minors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Permanent Account Number">
  <data key="d0">Permanent Account Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Permanent Account Number (PAN) is a unique identifier for individuals registered in the Income Tax department that Unity Small Finance Bank requires for account opening.&lt;SEP&gt;Permanent Account Number (PAN) is a unique identifier required for financial transactions in India, necessary for account opening at Unity Small Finance Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nomination Form">
  <data key="d0">Nomination Form</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">A Nomination Form is a document that indicates who should inherit the funds in a joint account or other financial accounts after the account holder's death.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nomination Form is a legal document that allows account holders to designate a nominee for their accounts in the event of their demise.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Identification Number">
  <data key="d0">Customer Identification Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Customer Identification Number is a unique number assigned to customers of Unity Small Finance Bank for account verification purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ORMD">
  <data key="d0">ORMD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ORMD refers to Operational Risk Management Department, which is responsible for overseeing risk management measures and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Head">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Head</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cluster Head is a senior position within the bank, responsible for overseeing specific geographic areas or segments within Unity Small Finance Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cluster Head is a senior official who must approve the premature closure of Term Deposits or other accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;A managerial position responsible for approving premature closure of term deposits or active accounts within Unity Small Finance Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audit">
  <data key="d0">Audit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Audit refers to the review and evaluation of a company's financial statements and compliance with laws and regulations to ensure accuracy and adherence to standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Finacle">
  <data key="d0">Finacle</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Finacle is a banking software solution used by Unity Small Finance Bank for operations and customer management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Turing">
  <data key="d0">Turing</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Turing is another banking software solution that Unity Small Finance Bank uses, updated in version 1.2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Risk Categorization">
  <data key="d0">Customer Risk Categorization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Risk Categorization is a process used by Unity Small Finance Bank to classify customers based on their risk levels, impacting the KYC and compliance processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Operating Procedures (SOP)">
  <data key="d0">Standard Operating Procedures (SOP)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) are documented guidelines outlining the processes and responsibilities for various banking operations, including account openings and closures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Individuals">
  <data key="d0">Individuals</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals are human customers who can open bank accounts in their names, either singly or jointly, and may require various documents for account verification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minors">
  <data key="d0">Minors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Minors are individuals under the age of 18 who can open savings or term deposit accounts, subject to conditions such as having a natural guardian or court-appointed guardian.&lt;SEP&gt;Minors refer to individuals under the age of legal adulthood who may have specific banking policies applicable to them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Politically Exposed Persons">
  <data key="d0">Politically Exposed Persons</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs) are individuals with prominent public functions in foreign countries, including heads of state and senior political figures, who may undergo additional scrutiny in financial processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs) are individuals who hold or have held prominent public positions, which places them at a higher risk for involvement in bribery or corruption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-013</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bank Official">
  <data key="d0">Bank Official</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Bank Official is a representative of the bank who conducts customer due diligence and oversees the account opening process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Heads">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Heads</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster Heads are bank officials responsible for approving exceptions, such as opening joint accounts with non-relatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FATCA Form">
  <data key="d0">FATCA Form</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">FATCA Form is a declaration form related to U.S. tax compliance that bank account holders must fill out if they declare multi-tax residency or non-residency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Officially Valid Documents">
  <data key="d0">Officially Valid Documents</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Officially Valid Documents (OVD) refer to specific identification documents accepted by the bank for customer identification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Declaration">
  <data key="d0">Self-Declaration</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A Self-Declaration is a document provided by customers to declare their address or other pertinent information in certain circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aadhaar Number">
  <data key="d0">Aadhaar Number</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">An Aadhaar Number is a unique identification number issued by the Unique Identification Authority of India, which is required for various banking and government services.&lt;SEP&gt;Aadhaar Number is an input field on the DOCZONE interface where users input the unique identification numbers assigned to customers in India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Account Opening Form">
  <data key="d0">Account Opening Form</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Account Opening Form is a document used by individuals to apply for opening a new bank account, requiring personal information and necessary documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;A document required for opening an account in a bank, containing rules and guidelines that must be understood by the account holder.&lt;SEP&gt;An Account Opening Form is a document that customers complete to initiate the process of opening a new bank account with Unity Small Finance Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;An account opening form from UNITY Small Finance Bank that includes various fields such as Customer Branch, Customer Name, DOB, and PAN No., populated with example data.&lt;SEP&gt;An account opening form associated with Unity Small Finance Bank Ltd, designed for capturing customer details and documentation necessary for KYC processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minor Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Minor Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Accounts specifically designed for individuals under 18 years of age, with specific documentation requirements based on the minor's age.&lt;SEP&gt;Minor Accounts are bank accounts opened for individuals under a certain age, often managed by guardians.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FATCA Declaration Form">
  <data key="d0">FATCA Declaration Form</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A form that must be signed by the guardian in front of bank staff, relevant for regulatory compliance related to financial accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thumb Impression">
  <data key="d0">Thumb Impression</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A biometric method used to authenticate the identity of illiterate or incapacitated persons when opening or operating bank accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visually Impaired Person">
  <data key="d0">Visually Impaired Person</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who has difficulty seeing but is not completely blind, capable of opening bank accounts under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mentally Ill Person">
  <data key="d0">Mentally Ill Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A mentally ill person is defined under the Mental Health Act, 1987 as someone who requires treatment due to a mental disorder, excluding mental retardation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="District Courts">
  <data key="d0">District Courts</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">District Courts are judicial bodies that serve as appointing authorities for guardians of mentally ill persons under the Mental Health Act, 1987.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collectors of Districts">
  <data key="d0">Collectors of Districts</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Collectors of Districts are administrative authorities responsible for appointing guardians for mentally ill persons in accordance with the Mental Health Act, 1987.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Savings Bank">
  <data key="d0">Savings Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A savings bank is a financial institution that allows individuals to open savings accounts, including accounts for mentally ill persons as per legal provisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Term Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Term Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Term deposits refer to fixed deposits offered by financial institutions where individuals can deposit money for a specified term, also applicable to mentally ill persons as per regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial products offered by banks that allow customers to deposit money for a fixed term at a specified interest rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Queer Partners">
  <data key="d0">Queer Partners</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Queer partners are individuals in a same-gender relationship who have the capacity to open joint bank accounts and nominate a partner according to banking protocols.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Politically Exposed Person (PEP)">
  <data key="d0">Politically Exposed Person (PEP)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Politically Exposed Person (PEP) is an individual who holds, or has held, prominent public functions in a foreign country, such as heads of state or senior government officials.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification within the checklist that indicates if the customer is a Politically Exposed Person, requiring additional scrutiny under due diligence processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-015</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UNITY Small Finance Bank">
  <data key="d0">UNITY Small Finance Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">UNITY Small Finance Bank Ltd. is a financial institution that provides banking services, including those tailored for various categories of customers like mentally ill persons, transgender individuals, and PEPs.&lt;SEP&gt;A financial institution offering banking services, from which the account opening form originates.&lt;SEP&gt;UNITY Small Finance Bank is a financial institution involved in banking services, particularly focusing on small finance.&lt;SEP&gt;A financial institution where the approval and decline decisions are made by key officers, reflecting a dual approach to business and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-021</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compliance Officer">
  <data key="d0">Compliance Officer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A Compliance Officer is a person responsible for ensuring that a bank adheres to legal and regulatory requirements, particularly regarding high-risk customers like PEPs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chief Business Officer">
  <data key="d0">Chief Business Officer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Chief Business Officer is a high-level executive responsible for overseeing the business operations and strategies of Unity Small Finance Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chief Business Officer is an executive role within a bank responsible for overseeing business operations and decision-making processes, including customer account approvals.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chief Business Officer is a senior executive responsible for overseeing business operations and making approval decisions regarding customer onboarding and risk assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;An executive role responsible for overseeing business operations and decision-making related to proposals at a financial institution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-021</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Branch Manager">
  <data key="d0">Branch Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Branch Manager is responsible for managing the operations of a bank branch, including recommending account openings for high-risk customers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Branch Manager is an individual responsible for approving customer profiles and overseeing the risk rating process at the bank branch.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Central AML Team">
  <data key="d0">Central AML Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Central AML Team is responsible for anti-money laundering compliance and monitoring within the organization.&lt;SEP&gt;The Central AML (Anti-Money Laundering) Team is responsible for monitoring and mitigating risks related to money laundering and ensuring compliance with AML regulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consumer Banking Team">
  <data key="d0">Consumer Banking Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Consumer Banking Team assists in managing customer relationships and banking accounts within the organization.&lt;SEP&gt;A team within Unity Small Finance Bank responsible for managing processes related to consumer banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-006</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CERSAI">
  <data key="d0">CERSAI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">CERSAI (Central Registry of Securitisation Asset Reconstruction and Security Interest of India) is responsible for maintaining KYC records and facilitating the retrieval of customer identification details.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EDD">
  <data key="d0">EDD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">EDD (Enhanced Due Diligence) refers to a set of processes and measures that banks implement to monitor high-risk customers more closely.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OVD">
  <data key="d0">OVD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">OVD (Officially Valid Document) is a document used to verify the identity and address of customers.&lt;SEP&gt;Official Valid Documents (OVD) refer to the documents required for identity and address verification in banking processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chief Compliance Officer">
  <data key="d0">Chief Compliance Officer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The Chief Compliance Officer is an executive responsible for ensuring that Unity Small Finance Bank complies with regulatory requirements and internal policies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chief Compliance Officer ensures that the bank adheres to regulatory requirements and internal policies, including those related to customer onboarding and risk management.&lt;SEP&gt;An executive role responsible for ensuring compliance with regulations and overseeing the approval or decline of cases at a financial institution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-021</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Identification Number (CIF)">
  <data key="d0">Customer Identification Number (CIF)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Identification Number (CIF) is a unique identifier created for each customer in the banking system, used for managing customer accounts and records.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Relationship Management Solution (CRM)">
  <data key="d0">Customer Relationship Management Solution (CRM)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Relationship Management Solution (CRM) is a software system used by Unity Small Finance Bank to manage customer data and interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BIDMS">
  <data key="d0">BIDMS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BIDMS (Bank Information Document Management System) is a digital document management system used by Unity Small Finance Bank to store customer documents and KYC records.&lt;SEP&gt;BIDMS refers to the banking IT platform used for managing customer data and documentation, particularly in the context of KYC and CKYC processes.&lt;SEP&gt;BIDMS refers to a process related to the banking system for managing customers, specifically minors, including steps for KYC and CKYC (Central KYC) data verification.&lt;SEP&gt;BIDMS is a specific section within the digital dashboard of Unity Small Finance Bank that is highlighted for its potential importance to users.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-drawing-002</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NSDL">
  <data key="d0">NSDL</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">NSDL (National Securities Depository Limited) is an organization in India responsible for the electronic storage of securities and for facilitating PAN verification processes.&lt;SEP&gt;National Securities Depository Limited (NSDL) is an organization that provides electronic depositories and services for the verification of PAN documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UIDAI">
  <data key="d0">UIDAI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">UIDAI (Unique Identification Authority of India) is the authority responsible for issuing Aadhaar numbers and managing Aadhaar verification services in India.&lt;SEP&gt;Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) is the authority responsible for implementing the Aadhaar scheme and validating Aadhaar documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC-AML Policy">
  <data key="d0">KYC-AML Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">KYC-AML Policy encompasses rules and regulations that govern the verification of customer identities and the prevention of money laundering activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Manager">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster Manager refers to the individual responsible for overseeing a specific group of branches within the bank, making decisions regarding account operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zonal Manager">
  <data key="d0">Zonal Manager</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zonal Manager is a high-level official in the bank responsible for managing and coordinating a particular geographic area or zone of bank branches.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Account (BSBDA)">
  <data key="d0">Small Account (BSBDA)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Small Account (BSBDA) is a type of bank account that allows customers to open an account with minimal documentation and restrictions on transaction limits, while enabling easier access for individuals without full KYC documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ongoing Verification Documents (OVDs)">
  <data key="d0">Ongoing Verification Documents (OVDs)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Ongoing Verification Documents (OVDs) are documents required periodically by banks to ensure that customer identification information remains current and complies with regulatory standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Experience">
  <data key="d0">Customer Experience</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Experience refers to the overall interactions and satisfaction level of a customer regarding the services provided by Unity Small Finance Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aadhaar (Targeted Delivery of Financial and Other Subsidies, Benefits and Services) Act, 2016">
  <data key="d0">Aadhaar (Targeted Delivery of Financial and Other Subsidies, Benefits and Services) Act, 2016</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Aadhaar Act enables targeted delivery of subsidies, benefits, and services through a unique identification system, facilitating access for customers seeking benefits or subsidies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CRM">
  <data key="d0">CRM</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Relationship Management (CRM) is a system used for managing a bank's interactions with current and potential customers, including handling of sensitive customer information.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CIF">
  <data key="d0">CIF</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Identification File (CIF) is a unique identifier assigned to each customer within the banking system, used for tracking customer information and transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;CIF stands for Customer Information File, which is a unique identifier used to manage customer data and accounts within Unity Small Finance Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;Customer Identification Number, a unique identifier for customers of the bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BSBDA">
  <data key="d0">BSBDA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account (BSBDA) is a type of bank account that offers basic banking services with certain conditions, including limits on transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CKYC">
  <data key="d0">CKYC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Central KYC (CKYC) is a standardized process for maintaining a single KYC record across multiple financial institutions, streamlining customer identification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CASA">
  <data key="d0">CASA</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Current Account Savings Account (CASA) refers to a type of banking account that combines demand deposits and saving elements, often used in the maintenance of customer accounts in banks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-attested Photograph">
  <data key="d0">Self-attested Photograph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A self-attested photograph is a personal photo signed by the customer, which is required for opening Small Accounts without documentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Information File">
  <data key="d0">Customer Information File</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Customer Information File (CIF) is a file created by the bank that contains information about a customer, including their risk profile and KYC (Know Your Customer) details.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Banking Operations-KYC/AML Cell">
  <data key="d0">Banking Operations-KYC/AML Cell</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Banking Operations-KYC/AML Cell is a department within the bank responsible for reviewing the risk ratings of customers and ensuring compliance with KYC and anti-money laundering policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Risk Profiling">
  <data key="d0">Risk Profiling</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk Profiling is a method used by the bank to assess and categorize customers based on their risk factors in relation to money laundering and other financial risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AML">
  <data key="d0">AML</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AML (Anti-Money Laundering) refers to the set of regulations and procedures intended to prevent the practice of generating income through illegal actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CKYCR">
  <data key="d0">CKYCR</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Central KYC Records Registry (CKYCR) is a database that stores KYC information of customers and is a part of the onboarding process to facilitate customer verification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retail Customers">
  <data key="d0">Retail Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Retail Customers are individual clients of the bank for whom initial profiling and risk assessments are conducted at the branch level.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entity Based Customers">
  <data key="d0">Entity Based Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Entity Based Customers refer to non-individual clients such as businesses or organizations whose profiling is scrutinized by the bank's branches and Centralized Account Opening Cell.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralized Account Opening Cell">
  <data key="d0">Centralized Account Opening Cell</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Centralized Account Opening Cell is a department within the bank that assigns risk profiles for Entity Based Customers after the initial profiling by branches.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Personal Information Sheet">
  <data key="d0">Personal Information Sheet</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Personal Information Sheet is a document filled by customers that provides necessary details for risk profiling including job, employer, designation, and income.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High Risk Customers">
  <data key="d0">High Risk Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High Risk Customers are those individuals or entities engaged in professions or activities with a high potential for money laundering risks, requiring more stringent KYC updates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medium Risk Customers">
  <data key="d0">Medium Risk Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medium Risk Customers are those whose risk profile requires periodic KYC updates every eight years, typically including high net worth individuals and commodity traders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Risk Customers">
  <data key="d0">Low Risk Customers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Low Risk Customers are those whose identities and sources of income are easily identifiable, requiring KYC updates every ten years.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Money Laundering Risk">
  <data key="d0">Money Laundering Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Money Laundering Risk refers to the potential risk levels that the bank may face based on customer relationships, influenced by various factors such as customer type and business activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Staff Benefit">
  <data key="d0">Staff Benefit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Staff Benefit refers to the eligibility criteria and entitlements for bank employees regarding additional financial benefits, particularly for retired and contract staff.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senior Citizen Benefit">
  <data key="d0">Senior Citizen Benefit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Senior Citizen Benefit is an additional financial benefit provided to retired staff who are classified as senior citizens.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Branch Change">
  <data key="d0">Branch Change</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Branch Change is the process through which a bank account holder can transfer their account from one branch to another, involving specific procedural requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Employee ID Card">
  <data key="d0">Employee ID Card</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Employee ID Card is a document used by bank employees for identification when approaching the branch to open an account or avail benefits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HR Operation">
  <data key="d0">HR Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">HR Operation refers to the human resource department responsible for verifying employee status and assisting with staff-related processes in the bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralised Processing Team">
  <data key="d0">Centralised Processing Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Centralised Processing Team is a department within the bank that handles the processing of branch change requests and other administrative tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CRM Application">
  <data key="d0">CRM Application</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">CRM Application is a software tool used by bank branches to manage customer relationships and process requests efficiently.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Current Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Current Accounts are a type of bank account designed for frequent transactions, providing flexibility and accessibility for account holders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">SOP - Account opening for Retail Customers.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1786619091</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
