  <data key="d0">tb-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-0013</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]sop_revision_updates_retail_accounts

This table presents updates made to the Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) related to customer risk categorization and account opening for retail accounts at Unity Small Finance Bank. It outlines specific revisions within SOP 1.3 and SOP 1.1, detailing the modifications and their effective dates. The first row details a revision in SOP 1.3 concerning customer risk categorization, specifically stating that all customers rated 'HIGH' require approval from the Business Head before onboarding. Additionally, it indicates that joint account holders must have their Know Your Customer (KYC) documents obtained and due diligence performed, with the new KYC retrieval process now involving the CKYCR Number to comply with audit requirements. The effective date of this update is noted as February 16, 2024. The second row outlines updates to SOP 1.5 based on the latest Operational Risk Management (ORM) comments, highlighting a process enhancement as advised by the Compliance Department, specifically the discontinuation of the customer profile verification (CPV) process in accordance with a recent RBI Circular from April 21, 2025. There are no totals or computed columns in this table, but it effectively illustrates the ongoing efforts by the bank to enhance compliance and operational efficiency. The surrounding context indicates that these procedures are part of a broader internal policy document designed to instruct employees on various responsibilities throughout the account opening process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2e34273750791ef213944c7971a5e5a1-mm-table-012</data>
