The table outlines the structure of account details for Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs) as maintained by Unity Small Finance Bank. It serves as a template for capturing critical information needed to assess and manage the accounts of individuals classified as PEPs, who hold or have held prominent public positions. The table consists of six rows and two columns, with the first column containing specific categories of information and the second column left empty, presumably for data entry. The rows include relevant sections such as 'Branch,' which identifies the specific bank branch managing the PEP account; 'Details of all accounts maintained with the Bank,' which pertains to the overall account management; 'Balance (for existing customer – as of ____),' designed to capture account balances; 'KYC (Y/N),' where KYC compliance is indicated; 'Match Category,' likely related to risk assessment classifications; and 'Details of the Match,' which would contain pertinent information regarding checks against compliance databases. The table thus provides a systematic approach to recording and monitoring information essential for the management of high-risk customers, ensuring that all necessary details are captured to meet regulatory standards. This is particularly crucial given the context of managing accounts for individuals who may pose heightened risk due to their political exposure.</data>
